I refactored `Pill` into a functional component backed by a new `usePermalink` hook, and updated `ReplyChain`, `BridgeTile`, and `pillify` to use named imports. I have not run the test suite.

Behaviour choices to check against the tests:
- The hook resolves synchronously with `useLayoutEffect` rather than `useEffect`. `pillify` mounts pills with legacy `ReactDOM.render`, so pills must appear in the DOM before `render` returns, as they did with the old class component.
- User pills in message context now render an `<a>` with `href` set to the url, as the spec requires. The old code set `href` to null for user pills.
- A user pill with no display name falls back to the Matrix ID.
- There is no default export any more. Any other file importing `Pill` by default will need the same one-line change. I could only see the files listed, so I could not check the rest of the repo.

