I've rewritten `Pill` as a function component and moved the link-resolution logic into a new `usePermalink` hook. I couldn't run anything, and the Pill and TextualBody tests check exact DOM output I couldn't see, so they may still fail.

- **Exports and imports:** `Pill.tsx` now has named exports `Pill`, `PillType`, `pillRoomNotifPos` and `pillRoomNotifLen`, with no default export. `ReplyChain.tsx`, `BridgeTile.tsx` and `pillify.tsx` now use named imports.
- **The `usePermalink` hook:** it works out the type, raw ID, text, avatar and click handler from `url`, `type` and `room`. It returns no type when it can't work one out, so `Pill` renders nothing.
- **What `Pill` renders:** a `<bdi>` around an `<a href={url}>` in messages (or a `<span>` elsewhere). Inside are the avatar when `shouldShowPillAvatar` is set, then the text, then a tooltip on hover.

Behaviour changes worth checking:

- **URL parsing:** links are now always parsed with `parsePermalink`, even outside messages; before, non-message pills used `getPrimaryPermalinkEntity`.
- **User pill links:** user pills in messages now keep the original link as `href`; before, the link was dropped and only the click handler remained. Clicking still opens the user view, because the handler stops default navigation.
- **User text before lookup:** for a user not in the room, the text shows the full Matrix ID until the profile lookup returns a display name. Before, it showed an empty string.
- **No tooltip on `@room`:** these pills have no URL, so they have no raw ID to show on hover.

